  "description": "Deploy the web service using the official **nginx:latest** image, naming the container **web_container**. It should start with the command `nginx -g \"daemon off;\"` and use an entrypoint of `sh -c`. Expose ports **80:80** and **443:443**, and mount the host directory **/var/www** into the container at **/usr/share/nginx/html** in read\u2011only mode. Set the environment variables **ENV=production** and **DEBUG=0**, and configure the container to always restart. Allocate **512** CPU shares, limit memory to **512\u202fMiB** with a swap limit of **1\u202fGiB**. Add the **NET_ADMIN** capability, drop **MKNOD**, run without privileged mode, and add an extra host entry mapping **myhost** to **192.168.1.10**. Tag the container with the label **com.example.description=Web service**.  \n\nFor the database, run the **postgres:13** image in a container called **db_container**. Provide the environment variables **POSTGRES_USER=admin**, **POSTGRES_PASSWORD=secret**, and **POSTGRES_DB=appdb**, and publish port **5432:5432**. Persist data by binding the host path **/var/lib/postgresql/data** to the same path inside the container. The service should restart **unless stopped**, has a memory limit of **1024\u202fMiB** and a swap limit of **2048\u202fMiB**, and uses the hostname **dbhost** within the network. It also runs without privileged mode."
